$DATUM 174501-65-6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Gewald Reaction Carbonyl compound (2 mmol),
malononitrile, or ethyl cyanoacetate (2 mmol) and sulfur (2 mmol) were
added in ionic liquid BmimBF4 or BmimPF6 (2 mL). The reaction mixture was
stirred for 3-8 h at 50°C. Reaction was monitored by thin-layer
chromatography (TLC). After the reaction, the resulting mixture was
extracted with Et2O (3 x 10 ml). The combined ethereal solution was
evaporated to give the crude product, which was purified by
recrystallization or preparative TLC (silica gel). After isolation of the
product, the remainder of the ionic liquids containing catalyst EDDA was
dried for 2 h under vacuum at 50°C. The next run was performed under
identical reaction conditions. Table 1, Entry 1, 4a, yield 71%. Mpa/°C:
139-140; Lit.mp/°C: 141-142[2a].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry-solvent, Gewald reaction, ionic liquid
used, reaction in BmimPF6 gave similar yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic reactions in ionic liquids. Gewald synthesis of 2-aminothiophenes
catalyzed by ethylenediammonium diacetate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hu, Yi; Chen, Zhen-Chu; Le, Zhang-Gao; Zheng, Qin-Guo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2004), 34(20), 3801-3806

