$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Thiophene 2-Amino-3-carbethoxy esters (2g-l) under Microwave
Irradiation: General Procedure B Step 1. A reaction mixture consisting of
the appropriate ketone (0.05 mol), ethyl cyanoacetate (5.7 g; 0.1 mol),
glacial acetic acid (3-5 drops), and ammonium acetate (0.4 g; 0.05 mol)
in 5 ml of ethanol was irradiated in a tall 100-ml beaker with MW at 350
W for 7-24 min. The water formed in situ got evaporated and deposited on
the top of the inner walls of the beaker, which were wipped off dry with
an absorbent tissue paper. The alkylidene ethyl cyanoacetate formed was
thiolated as such without isolation in the next step. Step 2. The crude
alkylidene ethyl cyanoacetate formed was dissolved as such in ethanol (4
ml) and to this sulfur (1.6 g; 0.05 mol) and diethylamine (3.67 g; 0.63
mol) were added. The reaction mixture was irradiated for 2 min at 350 W.
On chilling, the flask produced the desired product, which was filtered,
washed with chilled aq. ethanol, and dried.
2-Amino-3-carbethoxy-5,6-dihydro-4H-cyclopenta[b]thiophene (2g): Yield
7.0 g, 67%. mp 91-92°C; IR (KBr): 3414, 3296 (NH), 1649 (CO); 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ ppm: 1.30, 3H, t, CH3; 1.95, q, 2H, CH2 at 4; 2.5, m, 4H, CH2
at 4 & 5; 4.0, H, s, NH2; 4.29, 2H, q, CH2 at 3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient synthesis of substituted 2-amino-3-carbethoxythiophenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kathiravan, M. K.; Shishoo, C. J.; Chitre, T. S.; Mahadik, K. R.; Jain,
K. S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2007), 37(23), 4273-4279

