$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Amino-3-carbethoxy-5-ethylthiophene (2f): A reaction mixture of
n-butanal (3.6 g; 0.05 mol), sulfur (1.6 g; 0.05 mol), ethyl cyanoacetate
(5.7 g; 0.05 mol), and triethylamine (5.0 g; 0.05 mol) in DMF was
irradiated with microwaves in a similar fashion for 4 min. The reaction
mixture on cooling to room temperature was poured on an ice-water
mixture. The crystals obtained were washed with 20ml of chilled 50%
aqueous ethanol. The product (72% yield) with a mp of 72-74°C was
characterized as 2-amino-3-carbethoxy-5-ethylthiophene (2f).
2-Amino-3-carbethoxy-5-ethylthiophene (2f), yield 72% . mp of 72-74°C; IR
(KBr) cm-1: 3408, 3306 (NH); 1660 (CO); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm: 1.22, 3H,
t, CH3 at 5; 1.34, 3H, t, CH3 at 3; 4.2, 2H, q, CH2 at 3; 6.6, 1H, s, H
at 4; 4.2, 2H, s, NH2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient synthesis of substituted 2-amino-3-carbethoxythiophenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kathiravan, M. K.; Shishoo, C. J.; Chitre, T. S.; Mahadik, K. R.; Jain,
K. S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2007), 37(23), 4273-4279

