$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of thiophene 2-amino-3-carbethoxy
esters (2a-e) under Microwave Irradiation: General Procedure A An
appropriate ketone (0.05 mol), sulfur (1.6 g; 0.05 mol), ethyl
cyanoacetate (5.8 g; 0.05 mol), and diethylamine (3.65 g; 0.05 mol) were
mixed together in methanol (4 ml) in a 100-ml open tall glass beaker. The
beaker was irradiated with MW at 350 W for 2-5 min (Table 1). On
chilling, the reaction mixture produced the desired product, which was
filtered, washed with chilled aq. ethanol, and dried.
2-Amino-3,5-dicarbethoxy-4-methylthiophene (2c): Yield 5.9 g, 70.0%. mp
107-108°C; IR (KBr) cm-1: 3408.5, 3294 (NH); 1660.8 (CO); 1H NMR (CDCl3)
δ ppm: 1.32, 6H, s, CH3 at 3 & 5; 2.2, 3H, s, CH3 at 4; 4.32, 4H, s, CH2
at 3 & 5; 4.4, 2H, s, NH2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient synthesis of substituted 2-amino-3-carbethoxythiophenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
