$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Thiophene 2-Amino-3-carbethoxy
esters (2g-l) under Microwave Irradiation: General Procedure B Step 1. A
reaction mixture consisting of the appropriate ketone (0.05 mol), ethyl
cyanoacetate (5.7 g; 0.1 mol), glacial acetic acid (3-5 drops), and
ammonium acetate (0.4 g; 0.05 mol) in 5 ml of ethanol was irradiated in a
tall 100-ml beaker with MW at 350 W for 7-24 min. The water formed in
situ got evaporated and deposited on the top of the inner walls of the
beaker, which were wipped off dry with an absorbent tissue paper. The
alkylidene ethyl cyanoacetate formed was thiolated as such without
isolation in the next step. Step 2. The crude alkylidene ethyl
cyanoacetate formed was dissolved as such in ethanol (4 ml) and to this
sulfur (1.6 g; 0.05 mol) and diethylamine (3.67 g; 0.63 mol) were added.
The reaction mixture was irradiated for 2 min at 350 W. On chilling, the
flask produced the desired product, which was filtered, washed with
chilled aq. ethanol, and dried.
2-Amino-3-carbethoxy-4-(4-chloro)phenylthiophene (2j): Yield 5.0 g, 70%.
mp 102-104°C; IR (KBr) cm-1: 3450, 3333 (NH); 1660 (CO); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
ppm: 1.30, 3H, t, CH3; 2.35, 3H, s, CH3; 4.29, 2H, q, CH2; 4.0, 2H, s,
NH2; 6.3, s, 1H at 5; 7.3-7.5, 4H, ArH.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient synthesis of substituted 2-amino-3-carbethoxythiophenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
